    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:fb5db666cae6efb7",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "8b25243efd911627022cb2267c6948ff4698926996e0a34215bdbb06c175821c",
      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel. Today you will have an exciting adventure, navigating to small islands in the middle of the Strait of Magellan!\n\nMagdalena Island is home for the largest colony of Magellan penguins in the region of Magellan and the Chilean Antarctic. These Antarctic penguins were first met on the island about twenty years ago, and their numbers have been growing ever since.\n\nWhile walking around the island, you will have a unique experience of communicating with Magellan penguins very close to you. You will be able to see adult animals and their young (depending on the time of the visit). Not far from Magdalena Island is a smaller island, the rocky island of Marta. The island of Martha is home for a large colony of sea lions, which can be observed from a boat\n\nAt the end of the excursion, transfer to the airport for your flight to Santiago de Chile. Transfer to the hotel with a guide.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1J3iiKe3a157uLe4QAeKgqNdlhrMV3lAa",
